otoxic T lymphocytes specific for the simian immunodeficiency virus.</article-title><source>Immunol Rev</source><volume>170</volume><fpage>127</fpage><lpage>134</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10566147</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000823-Schmitz1"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmitz</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuroda</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Santra</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sasseville</surname><given-names>VG</given-names></name><name><surname>Simon</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Control of viremia in simian immunodeficiency virus infection by CD8&#x0002b; lymphocytes.</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>283</volume><fpage>857</fpage><lpage>860</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9933172</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000823-Yewdell1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yewdell</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Bennink</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Immunodominance in major histocompatibility complex class I-restricted T lymphocyte responses.</article-title><source>Annu Rev Immunol</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>88</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10358753</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000823-Chen1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Anton</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Bennink</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Yewdell</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Dissecting the